    {
      "question": "Where does a stem reader's seek land when it reaches the end of the stem?",
      "owner": "seek_clamp_or_end in src/audio/stem_reader.h",
      "owner_file": "src/audio/stem_reader.h",
      "owner_symbol": "seek_clamp_or_end",
      "date": "2026-10-10",
      "decision": "D107",
      "added_by": "so-t5a-review",
      "pattern": "\\bframe = std::clamp<int64_t>\\(frame,",
      "anchor": "frame = std::clamp<int64_t>(frame,",
      "must_match": [
        "frame = std::clamp<int64_t>(frame, 0, length_);"
      ],
      "must_not_match": [
        "if (seek_clamp_or_end(frame, length_, pos_, at_end_)) return;",
        "pos_ = std::clamp<int64_t>(frame, 0, length_);"
      ],
      "owner_lines": [
        {
          "file": "src/audio/stem_reader.h",
          "line_text": "frame = std::clamp<int64_t>(frame, 0, length);",
          "why": "seek_clamp_or_end, the owner"
        }
      ],
      "note": "Only a seek that assigns the clamp back to `frame` counts. A stream's own position (pos_ = std::clamp(frame, ...) in stream_mix.cpp and player.cpp) has no end flag to set and answers a different question. Decided by: derive-once review of so-t5a, finding 1 (2026-10-10); D107"
    }
